  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Quiet surface. Sharp mind.",
    "overview": "CrowbarOS keeps the approved Nullkeel blue-black field, controlled Ice signal, Rookslash crow and proportional Manrope interface. Engraved artwork supplies the identity's organic detail; functional controls remain quiet, precise and readable. This is an extension of that established world, not a replacement identity.\n\nThis root record combines shared brand commitments with the implemented Studio Settings surface: a native Linux desktop application built in Rust/GPUI on Wayland. The frontmatter's type, spacing and component values describe that native surface. The [brand-kit design system](docs/branding/crowbaros-brand-kit/DESIGN.md) remains authoritative for logo geometry, artwork, desktop concept compositions and the HTML review viewer. The [blueprint design system](docs/crowbaros-page/DESIGN.md) continues to govern the separate reading page. Their larger type scales, shadows and layout rules remain scoped to those surfaces.\n\nSources are [the canonical brand tokens](docs/branding/crowbaros-brand-kit/tokens/crowbaros.tokens.json), [native palette mapping](apps/studio-settings/src/theme.rs), [native controls](apps/studio-settings/src/main.rs), [product commitments](PRODUCT.md) and the [surface brief](.impeccable/surfaces/apps-studio-settings-src-main-rs.md). The first-build captures in [.impeccable/review/studio-settings](.impeccable/review/studio-settings/) establish the four appearance variants, compact layout, About, close protection and error placement. Current source includes the subsequent focus, native-title and error-copy corrections; those captures predate them. This document records implementation, not a final build or validation verdict. Follow the [finish review](.impeccable/review/studio-settings/finish-review.md) for that evidence.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Quiet opaque surfaces with a controlled signal for selection and action.",
      "Manrope for human-facing controls; IBM Plex Mono for technical data.",
      "Dark, Light and Warm Paper choices with a neutral Studio override.",
      "Familiar native window structure, explicit settings state and visible recovery."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Signal Rule",
        "body": "Use Ice for purposeful selection and action. Keep Steel decorative and use the palette's readable muted role for supporting text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Choice Rule",
        "body": "Preserve Dark, Light and Warm Paper as separate choices. Studio neutralizes the current window while retaining the underlying appearance choice.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Human Type Rule",
        "body": "Use Manrope for the interface and IBM Plex Mono for technical information. Use the supplied outlined logo master when a wordmark is required; typed UI text is not a substitute for that asset.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Stable Actions Rule",
        "body": "Keep the status and save/recovery actions reachable while the settings content scrolls.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The State Separation Rule",
        "body": "Distinguish focus from selection. Native buttons and theme cards use a dashed focused border; primary buttons use on-accent contrast for that border. A selected theme retains its solid border and “Selected” label when unfocused. Toggle rows use a solid focus border independent of their On/Off state.",
        "section": "shapes"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the approved Nullkeel colors, supplied Rookslash masters and established font families.",
      "Do pair filled accents with on-accent text and use each palette's dedicated focus color on pale surfaces.",
      "Do accompany selected and enabled states with visible labels, border treatment and switch position.",
      "Do keep the native footer reachable as content scrolls at the minimum window size.",
      "Do describe appearance as an app preview and desktop motion as an apply-on-Save preference.",
      "Do preserve the existing brand-viewer and blueprint design records within their own surfaces."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't replace the approved identity or redraw the wordmark from ordinary text.",
      "Don't use Steel for normal body copy or turn the accent into a large reading surface.",
      "Don't let focus disappear into a selected fill or border.",
      "Don't claim that neutral Studio chrome calibrates a display or themes third-party applications.",
      "Don't inherit concept-only controls, artwork treatments or web breakpoints as implemented native behavior.",
      "Don't treat component-preview HTML as evidence of native accessibility, final runtime validation or a web platform."
    ]
  }
